<title>SWITZERLAND: Audi sees profit rise in 1996.</title>
<headline>Audi sees profit rise in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>NEUHAUSEN, Switzerland 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Audi AG board member Franz-Josef Paefgen said on Thursday business was running satisfactorily in the first nine months of 1996 and it expected to post a profit &quot;that will be clearly better than last year&quot;.</p>
<p>For the entire year, Audi expected a single-digit rise in sales by volume, he told reporters at a joint presentation with Alusuisse about aluminium use in cars. Orders were doing well, and the new A3 model was &quot;doing magnificently&quot;, he said.</p>
<p>The Volkswagen AG unit posted a 1995 group net profit of 111 million marks on sales of 16.7 billion marks. It sold nearly 450,000 cars.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
